.TH AENIGMA-TOR-GET-AUTH 8 "2026-08-17" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-tor-get-auth \- print a previously generated onion service client access key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-tor-get-auth
.B \-s
.I SERVICE_NAME
.B \-u
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
.br
.B aenigma-tor-get-auth
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-tor-get-auth
prints to standard output the private client-authorization key previously
generated for a user of a given onion service by
.BR aenigma-tor-auth (8).
It performs no generation, modification, or restart of Tor; it only locates
and displays an existing key.
.PP
.B aenigma-tor-get-auth
must be run as root, since the underlying key file is owned by the
.I debian-tor
service user and is not readable by other accounts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " SERVICE_NAME"
Name of the onion service the key belongs to. Required.
.TP
.BI \-u " AUTHORIZED_USER"
Identifier of the authorized client whose key should be retrieved.
Required.
.TP
.B \-h
Display usage information and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
On success, prints a single line to standard output:
.PP
.RS
Access key: <onion-address>:descriptor:x25519:<base32-private-key>
.RE
.PP
This is the exact content of the client's
.I .auth_private
file, suitable for copying as-is into a client's
.B ClientOnionAuthDir
or Tor Browser's onion service authorization settings.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; the access key was found and printed.
.TP
.B 1
Invoked without root privileges, called with insufficient or invalid
arguments, the service's
.I authorized_clients
directory does not exist, or no key file exists for the given
.I SERVICE_NAME
/
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
pair.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients
Directory expected to already exist, created by
.BR aenigma-tor-auth (8).
Its absence is treated as Tor client authorization never having been
configured for this service.
.TP
.IB /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients/ AUTHORIZED_USER .auth_private
The private key file read and printed by this script. Must already exist.
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
This command prints unencrypted private key material directly to the
terminal. It performs no redaction, confirmation prompt, or secure
transport of its own \(em it assumes the operator is deliberately
retrieving the key for immediate, trusted use (e.g. relaying it to the
authorized client over a separate secure channel). Terminal scrollback,
shell history of any piped output, and screen-sharing sessions can all
expose the printed key; the operator is responsible for handling the
output accordingly.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
This script only checks for the existence of the service's
.I authorized_clients
directory, not for a fully valid onion service configuration in
.IR /etc/tor/torrc .
A stray
.I authorized_clients
directory left over from a removed or renamed service would still be
treated as configured.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aenigma-tor (8),
.BR aenigma-tor-auth (8)
